+# Auditor README V18.8
+
+This is an uncompiled source handoff. Begin with the V18.7→V18.8 change map, then review the new Yield Staking contract and Governance Token reservation replacement as one coupled system.
+
+## New review boundary
+
+`CurveYieldCyGovYieldStaking` depends on `CurveYieldGovernanceToken` for protected mint capacity. The intended fully backed-rate invariant is:
+
+`free held cyGOV + locked unused reservation >= effectiveMaxMintRate * 30`.
+
+Already accrued user liabilities are subtracted from held inventory. A checkpoint funds each liability before increasing reward-per-share. Allocation changes cannot reduce the minter below `mintedByMinter + reservedByMinter`. The Governance Token owner cannot directly cancel a protected rate-backing reservation, although immediate minter revocation can still halt future reserved mints and must be reviewed as an emergency-DoS surface.
+
+## Fee-routing rule
+
+All protocol fees go to Treasury except Revenue Staking's 10% fee on yield above benchmark, which is paid only to the address currently holding its `admin` role. Revenue Staking's separate 40% excess-yield fee goes to Treasury. Harvest caller incentives remain payments to the caller rather than protocol-fee recipients.
+
+## Immediate audit priorities
+
+1. Reservation replacement atomicity, protection, and accounting conservation.
+2. Reward-liability funding and held-first ordering.
+3. Max-rate behavior as reserved backing is consumed and future capacity unlocks.
+4. Initial 15B inventory-mint boundary.
+5. Lazy linear principal decay and epoch-extinction handling.
+6. Revenue Staking's 40% Treasury / 10% live-admin excess split, conservation, and sole non-Treasury fee exception.
+7. Deployment scripts and verifier consistency.
+8. Exact compiled runtime sizes.
+
+Static checks are not a substitute for compilation or executable tests.
