@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Threat Model V18.8
+
+## Assets
+
+- User cyvlSDT principal in Yield Staking and Revenue Vault systems.
+- Held and mintable cyGOV.
+- Protected mint reservations and global unlock capacity.
+- Reward-token flows through Revenue Staking and converter adapters.
+
+## Privileged/adversarial actors
+
+- Governance Token owner controlling minters and allocations.
+- Yield Staking owner controlling rates, Treasury, and initial inventory minting.
+- Revenue Staking owner/admin and notifier contracts.
+- Revenue Strategy/Converter owner and route adapters.
+- Malicious users timing stake, withdrawal, claim, or checkpoint interactions.
+- Malicious or non-standard ERC-20s and external adapters.
+
+## Principal failure modes
+
+1. **Unbacked max rate:** rate becomes active without 30 days of held/reserved capacity.
+2. **Reservation theft/release:** replacement frees old backing before securing new backing, or the token owner directly cancels protected backing.
+3. **Liability double counting:** accrued rewards remain counted as free held inventory.
+4. **Historical reward capture:** late staker receives rewards accrued before entry.
+5. **Decay misaccounting:** global index charges too much, too little, compounds, or strands old-epoch users.
+6. **Initial allocation bypass:** direct inventory mint consumes ongoing allowance as idle inventory.
+7. **Allocation undercollateralization:** owner reduces allocation beneath minted plus reserved commitments.
+8. **Fee split error:** benchmark/excess math loses value or charges more/less than 40%+10%.
+9. **Fee-recipient divergence:** the 40% Treasury portion or any other protocol fee misses Treasury, or the 10% admin portion reaches anyone other than the live Revenue Staking admin-role address.
+10. **DoS through minter revocation:** an existing protected reservation becomes unusable after emergency minter removal.
+11. **Rounding/dust lock:** reward or principal remainders become permanently unclaimable.
+12. **Privileged parameter DoS:** an extreme target-yield or max-rate value causes arithmetic or funding paths to revert.
+13. **Bytecode overflow:** expanded Governance Token or new Yield Staking exceeds EIP-170.
+
+## Expected invariants
+
+- Total supply plus total reservations never exceeds unlocked supply or hard cap.
+- Per-minter minted plus reserved never exceeds current allowance.
+- Protected Yield Staking reservations cannot be cancelled directly by the Governance Token owner.
+- Reward liability never exceeds cyGOV already held to satisfy that liability.
+- Free held balance excludes all unpaid liabilities.
+- User reward-per-share is checkpointed before share changes.
+- Total accounted principal falls by exactly the cyvlSDT sent to Treasury as decay.
+- `userAmount + treasuryAmount + adminAmount == grossReward` for every Revenue Staking notification.
+- Revenue Staking sends `treasuryAmount` to Treasury and `adminAmount` only to its current `admin` role.
